<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI25-ATMQA-002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI25-ATMQA-002" ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-07-25T09:19:48Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AICH-S5 ;
  triage:title "CLI trust mutation doesn't actually trigger the daemon refresh" ;
  triage:description "atm peer trust add/replace/revoke writes directly to PeerConfigStore and never signals a running daemon; refresh_https_trust is only reachable via the generic SIGHUP-driven reload_runtime_view hook, not \"after\" the CLI mutation as sprint Deliverable 4 states. Either wire the CLI to trigger reload directly, or correct the sprint doc's deliverable language to describe the actual (external-signal-required) design. FOLLOWUP (AICH-S5-FIX-1 recheck, a9e61fb0): escalated to Blocking. FIX-1 attempted closure by narrowing Deliverable 4's scope in the sprint doc rather than wiring the CLI trigger, but that rescoping was done unilaterally as part of a fix round without going through an explicit plan-change process -- a governance violation per standing policy (QA findings never rescope the plan; rescoping requires its own review). Additionally, the new live_trust_refresh_keeps_one_listener_reachable test added under AI25-ATMQA-001 calls refresh_https_trust directly rather than exercising the real CLI-to-signal-to-reload_runtime_view entry point, so the residual gap (ATM-QA-103/ATM-QA-005 signal-path coverage) is still unverified end-to-end. Both the improper rescoping and the residual signal-path gap must be resolved before this finding closes." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:category "ATM-QA" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
  triage:severity "Blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "crates" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-25T10:54:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:reassignReason "s26-s30 occurrences were stale snapshots recorded against an old headSha (b5eec1bf for s26-s29, 77252eca for s30) taken before those branches picked up the S5 fix (d6f7993a). Team-lead independently verified via git show origin/<branch>:crates/atm/src/commands/peer.rs at each branch's ACTUAL current HEAD (s26=28190ce1, s27=bed01b4d, s28=8e6c533a, s29=415a2db1, s30=9fd44444) that reload_runtime_view is present in all 5; quality-mgr independently re-verified the same 5 shas directly via git show. No merge-forward code work was needed -- the fix had already propagated; only the TTL records were stale." ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI25-ATMQA-002/s25/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI25-ATMQA-002/s25/2> ;
